WEBVTT

00:00:00.880 --> 00:00:02.350
Well, let's get crackin'.

00:00:02.350 --> 00:00:03.580
Let's-a-go.

00:00:04.030 --> 00:00:05.920
Stop messing around and start!

00:01:31.170 --> 00:01:31.750
'Kay!

00:01:31.750 --> 00:01:33.420
Everyone, have a seat!

00:01:34.490 --> 00:01:35.750
Happy New Year.

00:01:36.250 --> 00:01:38.090
The year just flew by, didn't it?

00:01:38.090 --> 00:01:39.510
Let's have another good'un.

00:01:39.680 --> 00:01:40.720
'Course...

00:01:40.900 --> 00:01:44.890
...I'll be biddin' farewell to some
of y'all in three more months.

00:01:44.890 --> 00:01:46.220
Guess who I'm talkin' about.

00:01:46.220 --> 00:01:46.850
Teacher!

00:01:46.850 --> 00:01:47.850
You don't mean me, right?!

00:01:48.020 --> 00:01:49.680
I can believe, right?!

00:01:52.350 --> 00:01:54.020
People always talk about the New Year's mood...

00:01:54.020 --> 00:01:56.400
...but I guess there's kinda a weird atmosphere.

00:01:56.400 --> 00:01:59.530
But it changes the second school starts.

00:01:59.530 --> 00:02:01.200
Unfortunately...

00:02:01.200 --> 00:02:02.030
Well...

00:02:02.030 --> 00:02:04.910
It's true that New Year's wields a mysterious power.

00:02:05.410 --> 00:02:09.370
Despite the fact that I spent the first three
days of the year busy working at home...

00:02:09.660 --> 00:02:11.460
...I gained weight!

00:02:11.460 --> 00:02:12.790
<i>New Year's magic, huh?</i>

00:02:13.670 --> 00:02:16.500
The cold weather makes it difficult to burn off your fat.

00:02:16.500 --> 00:02:18.090
I did a lot of moving around though.

00:02:18.090 --> 00:02:20.300
Three days of busy work as a shrine maiden.

00:02:20.550 --> 00:02:21.800
But you ate just as much, didn't you?

00:02:22.130 --> 00:02:22.840
Shrine maiden. New Year's food!

00:02:22.840 --> 00:02:23.550
Shrine maiden. Zoni soup!

00:02:23.550 --> 00:02:24.180
Shrine maiden. Snacks!

00:02:24.180 --> 00:02:25.300
Snacks! Snacks! Snacks!

00:02:25.300 --> 00:02:26.010
Shrine maiden. Snacks!

00:02:26.010 --> 00:02:27.060
Something like that.

00:02:28.100 --> 00:02:30.560
But the pictures of having fun during New Year's...

00:02:30.840 --> 00:02:31.680
...usually include badminton...

00:02:31.680 --> 00:02:32.730
...One Hundred Poets...

00:02:32.730 --> 00:02:34.810
...and kite flying...

00:02:34.810 --> 00:02:37.730
...but I've never actually seen someone do those.

00:02:37.730 --> 00:02:38.440
Well...

00:02:38.440 --> 00:02:42.150
These days, it's dangerous with
stuff like electric lines and cars.

00:02:42.150 --> 00:02:44.990
I just watched TV and read books.

00:02:44.990 --> 00:02:46.870
After those first three busy days.

00:02:47.050 --> 00:02:47.490
Um...

00:02:47.990 --> 00:02:49.790
I did those.

00:02:49.790 --> 00:02:53.800
I enjoyed badminton, One Hundred
Poets, and Pin the Tail on the Donkey.

00:02:53.800 --> 00:02:55.000
Doesn't match your image.

00:02:55.360 --> 00:02:57.540
My family follows western customs...

00:02:57.540 --> 00:02:59.960
...but our relatives in the country are more traditional.

00:03:00.440 --> 00:03:02.920
We wore kimonos and went
to the temple on New Year's...

00:03:03.170 --> 00:03:05.680
...and I had fun with my cousins.

00:03:05.680 --> 00:03:07.600
<i>An omnipotent god...</i>

00:03:08.250 --> 00:03:10.100
<i>Way more Japanese than I am!</i>

00:03:10.100 --> 00:03:11.220
<i>More traditional than my family!</i>

00:03:11.220 --> 00:03:12.770
<i>Wait, why Pin the Tail on the Donkey?</i>

00:03:13.200 --> 00:03:14.690
In One Hundred Poets...

00:03:14.690 --> 00:03:16.900
...they're all 31 syllable poems, right?

00:03:17.060 --> 00:03:17.650
Yes.

00:03:17.650 --> 00:03:19.070
You read out the first verse...

00:03:19.070 --> 00:03:21.570
...and look for the card with the rest of the poem.

00:03:21.570 --> 00:03:22.780
You must have skills...

00:03:22.980 --> 00:03:23.780
Not at all.

00:03:23.780 --> 00:03:25.360
I'm just a beginner.

00:03:25.360 --> 00:03:28.570
The expert snatch up the cards in a flash.

00:03:28.570 --> 00:03:29.530
Well, more like...

00:03:30.080 --> 00:03:33.800
I can't stand playing a game that
makes you feel like you're studying.

00:03:33.800 --> 00:03:37.630
People like you who view mental games as a
chore are why Japan's going down the drain.

00:03:37.980 --> 00:03:41.340
Why couldn't they use One
Hundred Poets for like a card battle?

00:03:41.340 --> 00:03:42.510
You could summon a monk.

00:03:42.510 --> 00:03:44.010
Think there was a Semimaru!

00:03:44.220 --> 00:03:46.340
Semimaru uses a shining attack!

00:03:46.340 --> 00:03:48.500
Ono no Komachi uses a lovely strike!

00:03:48.500 --> 00:03:49.760
Doesn't that sound fun?

00:03:49.760 --> 00:03:50.760
Back to your world, huh?

00:03:50.960 --> 00:03:55.170
But wouldn't more physical games
have helped you lose weight?

00:03:55.170 --> 00:03:56.140
Be quiet!

00:03:56.500 --> 00:03:58.150
It was those stupid rice cakes...

00:03:58.150 --> 00:04:00.310
Rice cakes are loaded with calories, aren't they?

00:04:00.730 --> 00:04:02.480
One as big as a matchbox...

00:04:02.480 --> 00:04:05.400
...is equivalent to a whole bowl of rice.

00:04:05.400 --> 00:04:08.030
Which means that Kagami's eating
a bowl of rice with each bite?!

00:04:08.030 --> 00:04:08.410
Hey!

00:04:08.410 --> 00:04:10.030
You also ate rice cakes, didn't you?!

00:04:10.610 --> 00:04:14.870
My mom's gone, so I've rarely
had zoni soup and that stuff.

00:04:15.220 --> 00:04:17.660
Actually, I don't really eat rice cakes.

00:04:17.660 --> 00:04:18.710
That's a waste.

00:04:19.020 --> 00:04:21.250
With zoni soup, sweet red bean
soup, soy flour rice cakes...

00:04:21.250 --> 00:04:23.590
There are so many fun ways to eat them.

00:04:24.290 --> 00:04:27.340
Looks like she's gonna lose to
the rice cakes again next year...

00:04:27.340 --> 00:04:28.270
...Kagami.

00:04:28.840 --> 00:04:32.310
What do you have to eat for New Year's...

00:04:32.310 --> 00:04:34.470
...instead of rice cakes, Izumi-san?

00:04:34.470 --> 00:04:36.350
Stuff like pizza and pasta.

00:04:36.590 --> 00:04:39.190
Our year starts with raw pasta.

00:04:39.810 --> 00:04:43.690
My dad cleans out the pasta
machine at the end of every year.

00:04:43.690 --> 00:04:44.570
Did you know?

00:04:44.570 --> 00:04:47.650
That thing rusts if you don't use it for a while.

00:04:47.650 --> 00:04:49.570
If you use it without cleaning it first...

00:04:49.570 --> 00:04:51.700
...the pasta ends up all black and stuff...

00:04:51.930 --> 00:04:53.950
So we clean it out...

00:04:53.950 --> 00:04:56.870
...and make pasta and pizza!

00:04:56.870 --> 00:04:58.460
Sounds very thorough.

00:04:58.460 --> 00:05:02.720
Well, Kagami's house probably orders
pizza and their pasta consists of cup noodles.

00:05:03.830 --> 00:05:04.920
More like...

00:05:04.920 --> 00:05:07.130
We don't have pizza or pasta on New Year's...

00:05:07.130 --> 00:05:07.840
No way!

00:05:08.230 --> 00:05:10.010
It doesn't go with traditional foods.

00:05:10.010 --> 00:05:10.930
Sure it does!

00:05:10.930 --> 00:05:13.140
It goes great with roast chicken!

00:05:13.140 --> 00:05:14.540
That's a traditional New Year's food?

00:05:14.540 --> 00:05:15.680
Sure it is.

00:05:15.680 --> 00:05:17.910
Under western traditions.

00:05:17.910 --> 00:05:19.270
That's how it works?

00:05:19.580 --> 00:05:22.690
What did you have for New Year's, Miyuki-san?

00:05:22.690 --> 00:05:23.770
Me?

00:05:24.020 --> 00:05:27.650
Your family sounds all wealthy and western...

00:05:27.650 --> 00:05:30.320
...so you probably didn't have
traditional stuff or rice cakes.

00:05:30.320 --> 00:05:32.700
Maybe you had like a full course French dinner!

00:05:33.010 --> 00:05:35.130
Not at all.

00:05:35.530 --> 00:05:37.330
I ate traditional foods...

00:05:37.330 --> 00:05:39.210
...and I was unable to bite through a rice cake...

00:05:39.210 --> 00:05:41.580
...and it stretched like whee!

00:05:42.990 --> 00:05:44.960
<i>What's with this walking pillar
to elements of turn-ons?</i>

00:05:44.960 --> 00:05:46.380
Rice cake goes whee!

00:05:46.730 --> 00:05:49.470
But New Year's goes by so fast.

00:05:49.840 --> 00:05:50.840
Yeah.

00:05:50.840 --> 00:05:52.720
Winter break goes by fast, too.

00:05:52.720 --> 00:05:54.800
It's supposed to be a long vacation...

00:05:54.800 --> 00:05:57.640
...but after cleaning, writing
New Year's cards, and homework...

00:05:57.640 --> 00:05:59.810
...you don't have much time to relax, right?

00:05:59.810 --> 00:06:00.850
Hold it right there!

00:06:00.850 --> 00:06:02.100
You didn't do New Year's cards this year!

00:06:02.100 --> 00:06:03.780
And you copied my homework yesterday!

00:06:04.510 --> 00:06:05.230
Oh, yeah.

00:06:05.230 --> 00:06:07.950
Did you have your first dream of the year, Kona-chan?

00:06:07.950 --> 00:06:10.900
Isn't it supposed to be a good
omen if you dream about certain things?

00:06:10.900 --> 00:06:11.800
Yep, yep.

00:06:11.800 --> 00:06:16.370
Usually, it's one: Mt. Fuji, two: hawk, three: eggplant.

00:06:16.370 --> 00:06:18.120
Officially, you would add...

00:06:18.120 --> 00:06:22.720
...four: fan, five: tobacco, six: blind man.

00:06:23.120 --> 00:06:25.080
It goes all the way up to six!

00:06:25.080 --> 00:06:25.920
But you know...

00:06:26.080 --> 00:06:28.880
Who ever dreams about that kind of stuff?

00:06:28.880 --> 00:06:29.780
What kind of dream would that be?

00:06:29.780 --> 00:06:31.130
And why a blind man?

00:06:31.130 --> 00:06:31.880
Pretty much...

00:06:32.160 --> 00:06:32.970
Hey.

00:06:32.970 --> 00:06:35.260
Do you have to dream about all of those at once?

00:06:35.260 --> 00:06:38.350
If all of those showed up in
your dreams, you'd be really blessed...

00:06:38.350 --> 00:06:40.770
...but I believe that just one will suffice.

00:06:41.040 --> 00:06:45.480
I thought you would have to dream about
a hawk twice and an eggplant three times.

00:06:45.680 --> 00:06:46.860
And quite frankly...

00:06:47.150 --> 00:06:50.400
Who really remembers what they dream about?

00:06:50.400 --> 00:06:53.780
People who care about that stuff are
having way too much fun with New Year's.

00:06:53.780 --> 00:06:54.490
You have a point.

00:06:54.890 --> 00:06:56.660
In my first dream this year...

00:06:56.660 --> 00:07:00.120
...I opened my shoe locker to find my shoes missing.

00:07:00.120 --> 00:07:03.910
So I had no choice but to take
shoes from someone else's open locker...

00:07:03.910 --> 00:07:06.970
...but the size was wrong.

00:07:07.330 --> 00:07:11.010
I looked up the meaning of this dream in
the encyclopedia for dream fortune telling...

00:07:11.010 --> 00:07:13.590
...and it said that it's a sign I am
pursuing skills useful to society...

00:07:13.590 --> 00:07:18.720
...but it will take a while before I accomplish that goal.

00:07:18.720 --> 00:07:22.820
The shoes apparently represent societal standing.

00:07:22.820 --> 00:07:23.890
Cheesecake?

00:07:24.270 --> 00:07:25.480
Miyuki-san's...

00:07:25.480 --> 00:07:26.980
...pretty ambitious.

00:07:26.980 --> 00:07:29.160
It's like I kinda understand, but kinda not...

00:07:32.600 --> 00:07:36.280
Another person was goofing off on the stage...

00:07:36.280 --> 00:07:38.530
...during the coming-of-age ceremony.

00:07:38.530 --> 00:07:41.700
Don't they realize they're representing Japan?

00:07:41.700 --> 00:07:44.460
Makes you wonder why they even bother going.

00:07:44.460 --> 00:07:45.330
No kidding.

00:07:45.690 --> 00:07:49.500
I wouldn't want to go to a
boring coming-of-age ceremony.

00:07:49.500 --> 00:07:52.210
<i>And this girl's gonna grow up to be a bad person.</i>

00:07:52.490 --> 00:07:56.220
What are you guys going to wear to your ceremony?

00:07:56.220 --> 00:07:59.220
Might as well go with a long-sleeve kimono...

00:07:59.690 --> 00:08:01.390
What about you?

00:08:01.390 --> 00:08:02.260
Well...

00:08:02.260 --> 00:08:05.820
My dad's probably going to
have me wear a long-sleeve kimono.

00:08:05.820 --> 00:08:06.810
I can see him doing that.

00:08:07.170 --> 00:08:07.680
Yahoo!

00:08:07.680 --> 00:08:08.270
But...
Yahoo!

00:08:08.580 --> 00:08:09.940
When you wear one...

00:08:09.940 --> 00:08:12.370
...you'd look more like a little kid going to the festival.

00:08:13.020 --> 00:08:13.860
Happy New Year!

00:08:13.860 --> 00:08:14.740
Hope ya had fun!

00:08:14.740 --> 00:08:16.700
Happy New Year, Cousin Yui.

00:08:17.070 --> 00:08:18.310
I haven't seen you in a while.

00:08:18.310 --> 00:08:19.990
Well, my husband was here.

00:08:19.990 --> 00:08:21.490
And a lot happens during New Year's.

00:08:21.490 --> 00:08:24.040
Oh, and my sister had a fever.

00:08:24.040 --> 00:08:25.580
She's got a weak body.

00:08:25.770 --> 00:08:26.750
Whoa!

00:08:26.750 --> 00:08:29.330
It definitely wasn't because I didn't
give her any New Year's allowance!

00:08:29.330 --> 00:08:30.920
Don't get the wrong idea!

00:08:30.920 --> 00:08:34.050
<i>Only a cop would reveal what she was
really thinking before I've said a thing.</i>

00:08:34.050 --> 00:08:36.420
A One Hundred Poets tournament
is currently underway...

00:08:36.420 --> 00:08:38.380
...and it's been one crazy ride so far.

00:08:38.380 --> 00:08:39.470
Oh, yeah.

00:08:39.780 --> 00:08:44.140
What did you do on New Year's when you were a kid?

00:08:44.140 --> 00:08:45.770
When I was a kid?

00:08:46.840 --> 00:08:48.850
Well, I did all kinds of stuff...

00:08:48.850 --> 00:08:49.730
Let's see...

00:08:49.730 --> 00:08:51.740
Um...

00:08:54.890 --> 00:08:56.820
Dot.

00:08:56.980 --> 00:08:57.450
Sorry.

00:08:57.450 --> 00:08:58.070
I forgot.

00:08:58.070 --> 00:08:59.490
No clue.

00:08:59.490 --> 00:09:01.950
<i>She really just goes with the flow.</i>

00:09:01.950 --> 00:09:04.290
<i>I've never heard her say anything serious.</i>

00:09:04.290 --> 00:09:06.000
Guess I outgrew my memories!

00:09:11.370 --> 00:09:14.090
Tsukasa's always cooped up
under the kotatsu these days.

00:09:14.090 --> 00:09:15.550
'Cause it's cold.

00:09:15.940 --> 00:09:17.090
I know what you mean!

00:09:17.090 --> 00:09:18.050
Kotatsus are so wonderful.

00:09:18.300 --> 00:09:21.510
Going to the bathroom's a pain though.

00:09:21.690 --> 00:09:22.730
Yep, yep.

00:09:22.730 --> 00:09:24.470
But you shouldn't say that so loudly...

00:09:24.850 --> 00:09:28.810
But we have a surefire way to
get a person out of a kotatsu.

00:09:29.060 --> 00:09:29.940
How does it work?

00:09:30.370 --> 00:09:31.190
Konata.

00:09:31.190 --> 00:09:32.940
If you stay under the kotatsu too long...

00:09:32.940 --> 00:09:34.360
...you'll get stuck.

00:09:34.790 --> 00:09:37.110
So your dad doesn't need a kotatsu.

00:09:37.110 --> 00:09:38.660
He likes them as much as the next person.

00:09:38.660 --> 00:09:40.070
It's just like a warning.

00:09:40.350 --> 00:09:44.000
'Cause we've both fallen asleep
together under the kotatsu before.

00:09:44.000 --> 00:09:45.280
I know what you mean!

00:09:45.280 --> 00:09:47.910
But they say that you'll catch a
cold if you fall asleep under a kotatsu.

00:09:47.910 --> 00:09:48.540
Yeah.

00:09:48.540 --> 00:09:51.370
So we turn it off once someone notices.

00:09:51.370 --> 00:09:55.180
It's like a mix of heaven and hell.

00:09:55.700 --> 00:09:57.880
Like right before you turn it on...

00:09:57.880 --> 00:10:01.430
...and after you turn it off, it feels even colder.

00:10:01.790 --> 00:10:03.220
I totally know what you mean!

00:10:03.800 --> 00:10:06.440
And doesn't it really suck when
you get out of bed in the morning?

00:10:06.760 --> 00:10:10.940
While we're at it, it's totally freezing after you
get undressed and before you get in the bath.

00:10:10.940 --> 00:10:13.770
But not enough to make you run.

00:10:13.770 --> 00:10:14.980
You might slip and fall.

00:10:15.220 --> 00:10:18.440
And doesn't it suck when you need to go
the bathroom in the middle of the night?

00:10:19.100 --> 00:10:19.860
I hate that!

00:10:20.100 --> 00:10:20.770
Hey.

00:10:20.770 --> 00:10:21.400
This is our stop.

00:10:21.820 --> 00:10:25.370
And the trip from the bus to the classroom is also hell.

00:10:26.400 --> 00:10:28.200
It's almost Valentine's Day.

00:10:28.360 --> 00:10:31.000
It always gets a lot more exciting this time of year.

00:10:31.000 --> 00:10:36.590
It kinda tickles me how everyone
can get so worked up every year.

00:10:36.860 --> 00:10:39.590
Having someone special on this day...

00:10:39.590 --> 00:10:40.890
...and confessing your feelings...

00:10:40.890 --> 00:10:42.170
...and having them reciprocated...

00:10:42.170 --> 00:10:43.880
...is a beautiful thing.

00:10:45.500 --> 00:10:47.350
You're such a girl.

00:10:47.350 --> 00:10:50.350
I just see it as a conspiracy by the chocolate industry.

00:10:50.900 --> 00:10:54.650
Well, I guess you could say it's
also a special time of year for me.

00:10:54.650 --> 00:10:57.610
They have a sale on the unsold chocolate afterwards...

00:10:57.610 --> 00:10:59.860
...so I'm looking for chocolate to use in making my own.

00:10:59.860 --> 00:11:02.070
And you, you have no dreams.

00:11:02.070 --> 00:11:03.820
Money can't buy love!

00:11:04.200 --> 00:11:05.200
At least, that's what they like to say...

00:11:05.200 --> 00:11:08.780
...but isn't Valentine chocolate a
way of showing love through money?

00:11:08.780 --> 00:11:12.250
I guess someone who's only
experienced love in games has some harsh views.

00:11:12.490 --> 00:11:18.300
Well, in games, it's all about upping
your relationship level before the day comes.

00:11:19.120 --> 00:11:22.720
I don't do anything special for Valentine's.

00:11:22.720 --> 00:11:23.760
Guys dream too much.

00:11:24.080 --> 00:11:26.930
Nobody managed to trigger the Kagami flag.

00:11:26.930 --> 00:11:28.470
What about you?

00:11:29.060 --> 00:11:30.100
I'm super popular!

00:11:30.500 --> 00:11:31.180
Right...

00:11:31.180 --> 00:11:32.600
In your game.

00:11:32.600 --> 00:11:35.850
When you talk about flags and relationship levels...

00:11:35.850 --> 00:11:37.730
...I seriously get worried about your future.

00:11:37.730 --> 00:11:40.190
You can't limit yourself to events in games.

00:11:41.310 --> 00:11:44.910
I can't stand those narrow-minded people
who don't know what they're talking about.

00:11:45.230 --> 00:11:46.160
So I'm wrong?

00:11:46.490 --> 00:11:49.730
Lately, events only take a few hours in game time...

00:11:49.730 --> 00:11:52.490
...so Valentine's Day is usually over in a flash.

00:11:52.490 --> 00:11:53.330
So what?

00:11:53.640 --> 00:11:57.170
But this year, I'm planning on
giving chocolate to someone.

00:11:57.710 --> 00:11:58.840
Seriously?!

00:11:59.330 --> 00:12:01.550
Someone playing the same online game as me.

00:12:01.980 --> 00:12:03.340
A friend from your game?

00:12:03.550 --> 00:12:04.800
You're giving it to him in person?

00:12:06.170 --> 00:12:09.060
I'm not actually going to meet the person.

00:12:09.670 --> 00:12:12.220
It'll be in-game.

00:12:12.220 --> 00:12:14.180
Since the characters are still human.

00:12:14.180 --> 00:12:15.770
Does that even count?

00:12:16.160 --> 00:12:18.310
So you just meant a game character.

00:12:18.310 --> 00:12:20.020
How dare you insult my bride!

00:12:20.600 --> 00:12:21.570
Bride?

00:12:21.570 --> 00:12:24.940
We're married in-game, and my character's male.

00:12:24.940 --> 00:12:25.530
What?

00:12:25.530 --> 00:12:26.570
Wait a sec.

00:12:26.570 --> 00:12:28.610
So the guy is giving the girl chocolate?

00:12:28.610 --> 00:12:31.280
And wouldn't it be like a girl giving a girl chocolate?

00:12:31.280 --> 00:12:32.870
If the other person's a girl...

00:12:32.870 --> 00:12:33.790
Don't worry.

00:12:33.790 --> 00:12:35.840
The other person's a guy in real life.

00:12:38.620 --> 00:12:41.250
Guess it doesn't matter as long as you're having fun!

00:12:41.250 --> 00:12:42.460
Got that right.

00:12:42.600 --> 00:12:44.590
I wanna go overseas.

00:12:44.590 --> 00:12:46.670
That came out of nowhere.

00:12:46.670 --> 00:12:48.970
Well, yesterday, Miyuki-san was like...

00:12:48.970 --> 00:12:50.630
Females giving chocolates on
February 14th is a Japanese custom.

00:12:50.630 --> 00:12:52.920
Miyuki-san!

00:12:52.920 --> 00:12:54.140
Females giving chocolates on
February 14th is a Japanese custom.

00:12:54.140 --> 00:12:56.100
In western society, people of both genders...

00:12:56.100 --> 00:13:00.110
...give chocolate and cards
to friends and people they like.

00:13:01.430 --> 00:13:02.520
That's what she said...

00:13:02.520 --> 00:13:05.820
...so a girl like me could still get lots of chocolate!

00:13:05.820 --> 00:13:07.490
I guess you could interpret it that way...

00:13:07.490 --> 00:13:09.110
...but you sure have a lot of confidence in yourself.

00:13:09.110 --> 00:13:10.740
Like you already know for a fact that you'll be popular.

00:13:10.740 --> 00:13:12.530
Don't worry.

00:13:12.530 --> 00:13:13.740
In foreign countries, little girls...

00:13:13.740 --> 00:13:14.660
Okay, stop!

00:13:14.660 --> 00:13:16.620
No risqué statements allowed!

00:13:17.170 --> 00:13:18.020
Uh...

00:13:18.020 --> 00:13:18.750
Will you accept this?!

00:13:18.990 --> 00:13:20.620
Happy Valentine's Day!

00:13:20.620 --> 00:13:22.550
Here, Kona-chan.

00:13:23.580 --> 00:13:24.840
Incredible wrapping...

00:13:24.840 --> 00:13:25.550
...for a uniform...

00:13:25.750 --> 00:13:28.170
And the inside's all cool and heart-shaped!

00:13:29.210 --> 00:13:30.720
I put some effort into it.

00:13:30.720 --> 00:13:33.140
Tsukasa's always enthusiastic about this kind of stuff.

00:13:33.140 --> 00:13:35.680
She was making them until morning.

00:13:35.680 --> 00:13:37.220
And it's only friendship chocolate.

00:13:37.420 --> 00:13:38.350
Tsukasa.

00:13:38.350 --> 00:13:40.730
You shouldn't give any friendship chocolate to guys.

00:13:40.730 --> 00:13:42.720
They'll definitely get the wrong idea.

00:13:42.720 --> 00:13:43.310
What?

00:13:44.110 --> 00:13:46.070
Anyway, here.

00:13:46.070 --> 00:13:48.360
Kagami's giving me chocolate!

00:13:48.360 --> 00:13:49.570
Tsukasa was making hers...

00:13:49.570 --> 00:13:50.820
...so I just joined in.

00:13:50.820 --> 00:13:51.450
You don't want it?

00:13:53.900 --> 00:13:58.910
Kagami looking like she's good at everything when she
actually sucks so she secretly works hard turns me on.

00:13:58.910 --> 00:13:59.540
Zip it!
Kagami looking like she's good at everything when she
actually sucks so she secretly works hard turns me on.

00:13:59.540 --> 00:14:00.580
Shut up and put it away.

00:14:01.810 --> 00:14:02.460
Huh?

00:14:02.940 --> 00:14:04.420
Kagami?

00:14:08.000 --> 00:14:08.840
Here.

00:14:08.840 --> 00:14:10.130
This is for you.

00:14:10.130 --> 00:14:11.550
Just so you know, it's a just friends thing.

00:14:11.550 --> 00:14:12.890
Friendship chocolate.

00:14:13.290 --> 00:14:15.850
S-Sorry the shape's funny.

00:14:15.850 --> 00:14:17.240
Silly.

00:14:17.240 --> 00:14:18.440
The shape isn't important.

00:14:18.440 --> 00:14:21.860
What matters is that you made it for me.

00:14:21.860 --> 00:14:23.230
S-Stupid.

00:14:23.230 --> 00:14:25.270
I told you it's not like that.

00:14:25.270 --> 00:14:26.770
Nothing like that?

00:14:26.770 --> 00:14:27.320
No.

00:14:27.320 --> 00:14:28.650
Just shut up and put it away.

00:14:28.650 --> 00:14:29.940
This is my first time.

00:14:29.940 --> 00:14:31.030
The first time's most important.

00:14:31.300 --> 00:14:33.530
So did you give anybody chocolate, Miyuki-san?

00:14:33.810 --> 00:14:36.780
I gave chocolate to my father and a relative.

00:14:36.780 --> 00:14:40.120
I gave chocolate to everybody I'm friendly with.

00:14:40.280 --> 00:14:42.330
I gave chocolate to you, Tsukasa, and Miyuki.

00:14:42.530 --> 00:14:43.500
Sheesh.

00:14:43.500 --> 00:14:45.460
You guys sure had a boring St. Valentine's Day.

00:14:45.710 --> 00:14:48.050
Don't need to hear it from
someone who lives in an online game.

00:14:49.830 --> 00:14:50.800
Oh, yeah.

00:14:50.800 --> 00:14:53.440
Your cousin was accepted to Ryouou, right?

00:14:53.440 --> 00:14:54.380
She was.

00:14:54.380 --> 00:14:56.260
It's pretty far from her home...

00:14:56.260 --> 00:14:58.220
...so she'll be living with us starting next month.

00:14:58.220 --> 00:15:00.390
She's always been like a little sister anyway...

00:15:00.390 --> 00:15:01.930
...so we've been in touch.

00:15:01.930 --> 00:15:02.430
Really.

00:15:02.750 --> 00:15:04.190
But next to you...

00:15:04.190 --> 00:15:06.150
...nobody would be able to tell who's younger.

00:15:06.460 --> 00:15:07.310
No, like I said...

00:15:07.310 --> 00:15:09.980
She's like a little sister in more ways than one.

00:15:09.980 --> 00:15:11.150
<i>She's that small?!</i>

00:15:11.470 --> 00:15:13.360
But if she got accepted to our school...

00:15:13.360 --> 00:15:15.320
...your cousin must be really smart.

00:15:15.320 --> 00:15:18.030
That just sounds like you're
being really presumptuous.

00:15:18.030 --> 00:15:18.870
Since you're a student here.

00:15:19.070 --> 00:15:22.260
But I barely passed the exam.

00:15:22.260 --> 00:15:23.420
Exams, huh?

00:15:23.420 --> 00:15:26.220
We'll be taking our exams next year.

00:15:26.620 --> 00:15:28.730
Guess I'll be spending the whole year studying.

00:15:28.730 --> 00:15:29.340
Sounds awful.

00:15:29.670 --> 00:15:30.500
Exams...

00:15:30.500 --> 00:15:31.510
Should I even take them?

00:15:31.510 --> 00:15:33.470
I haven't even picked a major.

00:15:33.470 --> 00:15:35.590
You seriously need to start thinking about your future.

00:15:36.790 --> 00:15:40.640
Studying, manual labor, and me just don't mix.

00:15:40.640 --> 00:15:43.310
What kind of future do you have in mind?

00:15:43.310 --> 00:15:43.550
<i>Use a hobby to make profit and make games...</i>

00:15:43.550 --> 00:15:46.400
<i>I design games. 'Cause it's my hobby.</i>

00:15:46.400 --> 00:15:46.930
<i>Be a self-proclaimed manga
artist who can only sell at Comiket...</i>

00:15:46.930 --> 00:15:49.110
<i>Megas smoked cheese-nyoro.</i>

00:15:49.440 --> 00:15:49.810
<i>Or perhaps, indulge your curiosity
and become a professional writer.</i>

00:15:49.810 --> 00:15:51.610
<i>There can only be one truth!</i>

00:15:51.610 --> 00:15:52.190
<i>And this isn't it!</i>
<i>Or perhaps, indulge your curiosity
and become a professional writer.</i>

00:15:52.190 --> 00:15:52.570
<i>And this isn't it!</i>

00:15:52.570 --> 00:15:55.820
<i>No, maybe just a novelist who aims for a niche market.</i>

00:15:56.080 --> 00:15:58.900
<i>Since you like computers,
I guess art design might work.</i>

00:15:59.270 --> 00:16:03.250
<i>Maybe a scenario writer who uses
random material instead of an actual story writer.</i>

00:16:03.250 --> 00:16:04.410
<i>Or she doesn't go to college...</i>

00:16:04.800 --> 00:16:07.000
<i>Or they're all the same thing?!</i>

00:16:07.000 --> 00:16:07.920
What?

00:16:11.940 --> 00:16:12.380
What is it?

00:16:12.930 --> 00:16:13.900
Manager!

00:16:13.900 --> 00:16:15.760
Legendary Girl A...

00:16:15.760 --> 00:16:17.050
...has returned!

00:16:17.920 --> 00:16:19.640
What?!

00:16:20.110 --> 00:16:22.200
She shook us off last time!

00:16:22.200 --> 00:16:23.930
Manager!

00:16:23.930 --> 00:16:25.850
Today!

00:16:26.510 --> 00:16:31.440
We will absolutely make sure she
reaches the goal known as our register!

00:16:32.100 --> 00:16:32.650
Giro.

00:16:33.080 --> 00:16:35.160
She seems to be at a loss.

00:16:35.640 --> 00:16:36.860
Then allow us to...

00:16:36.860 --> 00:16:39.160
...help her find her way!

00:16:39.700 --> 00:16:40.570
Okay, everyone!

00:16:40.570 --> 00:16:41.370
Let 'er rip!

00:16:41.370 --> 00:16:41.830
Okay!

00:16:41.830 --> 00:16:42.530
Let's go!

00:16:42.530 --> 00:16:42.830
Yeah!

00:16:42.830 --> 00:16:43.450
Let's go!

00:16:43.450 --> 00:16:43.830
Yeah!

00:16:43.830 --> 00:16:44.660
Let's go!

00:16:44.660 --> 00:16:45.660
Aw yeah!

00:16:47.970 --> 00:16:48.810
Manager.

00:16:48.810 --> 00:16:52.040
Attempting to determine Legendary
Girl A's objective for the day.

00:16:52.470 --> 00:16:52.930
Okay.

00:16:52.930 --> 00:16:53.420
Countin' on you.

00:16:53.880 --> 00:16:55.050
What's the newest comic out?

00:16:55.050 --> 00:16:55.920
Yes.

00:16:55.920 --> 00:16:57.130
Volume 14 of Sgt. Frog, sah!

00:16:57.400 --> 00:16:58.180
Okay!

00:16:58.180 --> 00:16:59.720
Raise the height of our goods to the appropriate level...

00:16:59.720 --> 00:17:01.010
...to bring them to the attention of Legendary Girl A!

00:17:01.010 --> 00:17:01.720
Okay!

00:17:01.720 --> 00:17:03.350
And deploy the flyers!

00:17:03.350 --> 00:17:04.310
Tama!

00:17:05.090 --> 00:17:06.230
Deployment complete!

00:17:06.230 --> 00:17:07.310
Sah!

00:17:07.310 --> 00:17:08.190
Okay.

00:17:08.190 --> 00:17:10.330
Keep an eye on her movements.

00:17:10.330 --> 00:17:12.940
And as Legendary Girl A approaches the register...

00:17:12.940 --> 00:17:14.900
...deploy our best-selling goods!

00:17:14.900 --> 00:17:15.860
Roger!

00:17:15.860 --> 00:17:16.820
Sah!

00:17:18.840 --> 00:17:19.580
Okay.

00:17:20.360 --> 00:17:21.200
Manager!

00:17:21.200 --> 00:17:24.280
Legendary Girl A's objective isn't the comics section!

00:17:24.600 --> 00:17:25.620
What?!

00:17:26.780 --> 00:17:27.540
Manager.

00:17:27.540 --> 00:17:29.790
Switch target to the DVD section.

00:17:29.790 --> 00:17:30.670
Okay.

00:17:30.670 --> 00:17:32.040
Just to be sure...

00:17:32.040 --> 00:17:35.340
...block all side paths so Legendary Girl A...

00:17:35.340 --> 00:17:36.710
...heads straight to the new DVD section!

00:17:36.710 --> 00:17:37.420
Roger!

00:17:37.420 --> 00:17:38.130
Sah!

00:17:38.790 --> 00:17:40.470
So sorry!

00:17:40.670 --> 00:17:42.390
Tama! Tama!

00:17:42.820 --> 00:17:43.800
Oh, my!

00:17:43.800 --> 00:17:45.680
Forgive me!

00:17:45.680 --> 00:17:47.850
Gero-gero-gero-gero build-up!
Tama-tama-tama-tama build-up!

00:17:49.340 --> 00:17:51.190
Okay, okay...

00:17:57.100 --> 00:17:58.700
Manager!

00:17:58.700 --> 00:18:00.740
She's...

00:18:00.840 --> 00:18:03.480
...picked up the item!

00:18:03.480 --> 00:18:06.650
I've finally become a winner today!

00:18:06.650 --> 00:18:07.490
Comrades!

00:18:07.490 --> 00:18:09.870
Let us have a wild celebration tonight!

00:18:09.870 --> 00:18:10.370
Yes!

00:18:10.370 --> 00:18:11.330
Sah!

00:18:12.530 --> 00:18:14.080
It was a feint!

00:18:23.460 --> 00:18:24.850
I'll have to bring out my trump card!

00:18:29.170 --> 00:18:29.930
Come...

00:18:29.930 --> 00:18:34.320
Bring that bargain, super-rare,
out-of-print DVD to me.

00:18:36.310 --> 00:18:37.110
Manager.

00:18:37.110 --> 00:18:38.230
She is heading for the register.

00:18:38.480 --> 00:18:39.280
Okay.

00:18:39.280 --> 00:18:40.440
Keep going!

00:18:42.310 --> 00:18:43.950
What a beautiful scene!

00:18:43.950 --> 00:18:46.700
The crowd inside me is
cheering with applause right now!

00:18:46.700 --> 00:18:47.530
We did it!

00:18:47.530 --> 00:18:48.040
Sah!

00:18:48.910 --> 00:18:51.040
Your total comes to 1,785 yen.

00:19:02.300 --> 00:19:03.510
I'm short 3 yen.

00:19:06.210 --> 00:19:07.010
Sorry.

00:19:07.010 --> 00:19:09.360
Please put that back.

00:19:14.850 --> 00:19:16.020
We'll be back!

00:19:21.800 --> 00:19:22.990
Good lucky!

00:19:23.220 --> 00:19:23.870
Okay!

00:19:23.870 --> 00:19:25.860
Let's kick this into gear!

00:19:25.860 --> 00:19:29.910
We're already on the thirteenth
episode of Lucky Channel!

00:19:29.910 --> 00:19:30.370
Okay.

00:19:30.370 --> 00:19:33.580
As you already know, I'm
your navigator, Akira Kogami!

00:19:33.580 --> 00:19:34.540
And...

00:19:34.830 --> 00:19:35.270
Yes.

00:19:35.270 --> 00:19:35.370
D-D-Drill!

00:19:35.370 --> 00:19:37.370
I'm Akira-sama's assistant, Minoru Shiraishi.

00:19:37.370 --> 00:19:37.500
D-D-Drill!

00:19:37.500 --> 00:19:39.170
It's a pleasure!

00:19:39.170 --> 00:19:40.440
That's right.

00:19:40.440 --> 00:19:41.430
We're on episode 13.

00:19:41.430 --> 00:19:41.800
D-D-D-D-Drill!

00:19:41.800 --> 00:19:43.300
Into the second season.

00:19:43.300 --> 00:19:43.740
D-D-Drill!

00:19:43.740 --> 00:19:45.210
It's like we've reached the
fifth station on Mt. Fuji, right?

00:19:45.210 --> 00:19:49.020
D-D-Drill!

00:19:49.390 --> 00:19:50.220
Mt. Fuji?

00:19:50.220 --> 00:19:52.730
You can drive up to the fifth station.

00:19:53.420 --> 00:19:54.600
That's true...

00:19:55.250 --> 00:19:55.640
That's right!

00:19:55.930 --> 00:19:58.150
I've climbed Mt. Takao before!

00:19:58.700 --> 00:20:00.700
Don't you have something else to talk about?

00:20:00.700 --> 00:20:00.820
That's true...

00:20:00.820 --> 00:20:02.280
D-D-D-D-D-D-D-D-Drill!

00:20:02.280 --> 00:20:03.900
Man, uh...

00:20:03.900 --> 00:20:05.570
Akira-sama's twin drills look wonderful!

00:20:05.930 --> 00:20:08.120
What's so wonderful about them?

00:20:08.610 --> 00:20:10.530
The way they go round and round like a shell.

00:20:12.280 --> 00:20:13.470
Well...

00:20:13.470 --> 00:20:14.660
Uh...

00:20:14.660 --> 00:20:16.000
We have a special announcement today.

00:20:16.540 --> 00:20:19.580
The results for the Lucky Star figure poll!

00:20:19.580 --> 00:20:22.680
Let's have Akira-sama announce the results!

00:20:23.080 --> 00:20:24.720
The characters that will soon
be getting figures are Konata Izumi...

00:20:24.720 --> 00:20:27.010
Akira-sama, do a proper job!
The characters that will soon
be getting figures are Konata Izumi...

00:20:27.010 --> 00:20:28.300
Congratulations!

00:20:28.680 --> 00:20:30.350
Sheesh, everybody knew this would happen.

00:20:30.350 --> 00:20:31.850
What a joke.

00:20:32.390 --> 00:20:33.050
No, no, no...

00:20:33.050 --> 00:20:34.690
Just means that the higher-ups think the
actual show is more important than this corner.
No, no, no...

00:20:34.690 --> 00:20:37.850
Just means that the higher-ups think the
actual show is more important than this corner.

00:20:37.850 --> 00:20:40.070
Of course not, right?

00:20:42.060 --> 00:20:42.610
Look.

00:20:42.610 --> 00:20:44.070
The producers agree.

00:20:44.400 --> 00:20:45.570
Yeah.

00:20:45.570 --> 00:20:47.320
I'll just fall for your little trick.

00:20:47.320 --> 00:20:49.030
I'm already used to being backstabbed.

00:20:49.450 --> 00:20:50.780
Little trick?

00:20:50.780 --> 00:20:52.640
That's an awful thing to say.

00:20:52.640 --> 00:20:58.050
And don't tell me that it says
you're going to have a figure made.

00:20:58.370 --> 00:20:59.040
Of course not!

00:20:59.290 --> 00:20:59.620
Okay.

00:20:59.620 --> 00:21:02.160
We'll be making a figure of Konata Izumi-san this time.

00:21:02.160 --> 00:21:04.910
And the popular Minoru Shiraishi will also get a figure?!

00:21:05.400 --> 00:21:07.010
The hell is this?!

00:21:07.010 --> 00:21:08.810
U-Uh...

00:21:09.170 --> 00:21:11.280
It's time to say goodbye!

00:21:11.280 --> 00:21:16.690
So please send us any suggestions
or comments you have!

00:21:16.690 --> 00:21:18.600
You can leave them on our home page.

00:21:19.020 --> 00:21:20.520
Right, Akira-sama?

00:21:20.790 --> 00:21:21.690
Er, what?
I'm leaving.

00:21:21.690 --> 00:21:23.360
W-Wait!

00:21:23.890 --> 00:21:25.860
B-Bye-bee!

00:21:25.860 --> 00:21:26.280
Akira-sama!

00:21:26.530 --> 00:21:26.770
Wait up!

00:21:26.770 --> 00:21:27.440
Okay.

00:21:27.440 --> 00:21:27.570
All the staff members can go home.
Okay.
Wait up!

00:21:27.570 --> 00:21:28.490
All the staff members can go home.

00:21:28.490 --> 00:21:29.150
D-Drill!

00:23:00.890 --> 00:23:03.150
Well, next time on Sgt. Frog:

00:23:03.150 --> 00:23:03.980
No!

00:23:03.980 --> 00:23:05.900
You mean next time on Lucky Star!

00:23:05.900 --> 00:23:06.690
Giro-giro.

00:23:06.690 --> 00:23:08.740
Comrade, I have a good idea!

00:23:09.110 --> 00:23:11.990
Japanese anime is now a global industry.

00:23:11.990 --> 00:23:14.580
If we use it to brainwash the people on Pekopon...

00:23:14.580 --> 00:23:16.540
...we can complete the invasion
of Pekopon in no time, sah!

00:23:16.540 --> 00:23:19.080
You're a genius, Sarge!

00:23:19.080 --> 00:23:20.080
Worthless.

00:23:20.080 --> 00:23:22.540
A soldier should act like a soldier and use brute force!

00:23:22.540 --> 00:23:24.180
Shut your mouth, you red dharma doll!

00:23:24.740 --> 00:23:28.010
In this age, whoever controls
information controls the battle!

00:23:28.010 --> 00:23:30.720
Well, your prehistoric mind wouldn't understand that.

00:23:30.720 --> 00:23:32.510
You better watch yourself!

00:23:32.510 --> 00:23:33.010
In any case...

00:23:33.680 --> 00:23:34.260
Next time:

00:23:34.260 --> 00:23:35.560
Under One Roof.

00:23:35.560 --> 00:23:36.850
Look forward to next time!

00:23:36.850 --> 00:23:38.190
G-Gero!
